To determine how many pieces of wire Tracy obtained, we start by converting the total length of the wire from feet to inches, since the lengths of the pieces are given in inches.

---

### Step 1: Convert total length to inches
We are told that the wire was 4 feet long. Since 1 foot equals 12 inches:

$$
\text{Total wire length} = 4 \, \text{feet} \times 12 \, \text{inches/foot} = 48 \, \text{inches}
$$

---

### Step 2: Divide total length by the length of each piece
Each piece is 6 inches long. To find the number of pieces, divide the total length by the length of each piece:

$$
\text{Number of pieces} = \frac{48 \, \text{inches}}{6 \, \text{inches/piece}} = 8
$$

---

### Conclusion
Tracy obtained exactly 8 pieces of 6-inch long wire from the 4-feet long wire.

$$
\boxed{8}
$$

